(footprint "Samtec_BCS-112-S-D-HE"
	(version 20241229)
	(generator "aqroot-beta-library")
	(generator_version "10.0")
	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "Samtec BCS-112-S-D-HE community expansion connector, 2 x 12 = 24 contacts, .100 in / 2.54 mm pitch, FEMALE Tiger Claw dual-beam pass-through socket strip, HORIZONTAL (right-angle) entry, through-hole, 30 uin selective gold. Land pattern reproduced from the Samtec RECOMMENDED PCB LAYOUT drawing BCS-1XX-XXX-X-XX-XXX FOOTPRINT, REVISION B, FIG 3 (BCS-1XX-XXX-D-HE-XXX), verified 2026-08-23: pitch within a row .100 in / 2.54 mm; ROW-TO-ROW .310 +/-.002 in = 7.87 +/-0.05 mm; hole .028 in = 0.71 mm PTH; pin-field length = positions x 2.54 - 2.54 = 27.94 mm for 12 positions. THIS IS NOT INTERCHANGEABLE WITH A VERTICAL 2x12 PATTERN, whose rows sit 2.54 mm apart. Odd pins are row A, even pins are row B (D-084). Pad 1 is rectangular. Body 30.48 (L) x 8.13 (D) x 5.33 (H) mm; the mating face points along -Y, i.e. toward the enclosure wall. 4.6 A per contact mated with TSW, 450 VAC / 636 VDC, -55 to +125 C, UL E111594, halogen free, MSL 1. BCS-112-L-D-HE (10 uin gold) is a plating-only alternate with an identical body and an identical footprint - but only 100 mating cycles against the -S option's 2500 (Samtec 187544 Rev 1), which is why -S is locked. THE ENCLOSURE SUPPLIES POLARISATION AND KEYING (D-097): there is no electrical key contact.")
	(tags "connector samtec BCS 2x12 24 contact 2.54mm socket horizontal right-angle through-hole community port")
	(attr through_hole)
